#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:652
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Troubleshooting Journaling"
msgstr "日志功能故障排除"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:655
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following section covers frequently asked questions regarding problems "
"related to journaling."
msgstr "以下部分介绍与日志功能相关问题的常见问答。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:656
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "I am experiencing kernel panics during periods of high disk activity. Is this related to GEOM journaling?"
msgstr "磁盘活动繁忙时系统会发生内核崩溃。这与 GEOM 日志有关吗？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:659
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On modern FreeBSD systems, kernel panics caused solely by an undersized GEOM "
"journal are rare."
msgstr "在现代 FreeBSD 系统中，单纯由 GEOM 日志空间不足导致的内核崩溃很少见。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:662
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Under sustained or burst-heavy write workloads, an undersized journal "
"typically results in write throttling or temporary I/O stalls while the "
"journal is flushed to the data provider.  A kernel panic may occur only in "
"exceptional cases, usually in combination with additional problems such as I/"
"O errors or resource exhaustion, where continuing operation could risk file "
"system integrity."
msgstr "在持续写入或突发写入负载下，日志空间不足通常会导致写入限流，或在日志刷新到数据提供者期间出现暂时的 I/O 停顿。只有在极少数情况下才可能发生内核崩溃，通常还伴有 I/O 错误或资源耗尽等其他问题；在这些情况下，继续运行可能会危及文件系统完整性。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:664
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If panics are observed during heavy write activity, increasing the size of "
"the journal provider for the affected file system is recommended."
msgstr "如果在大量写入期间发生内核崩溃，建议增大受影响文件系统的日志提供者容量。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:665
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "I made some mistake during configuration, and I cannot boot normally now. Can this be fixed some way?"
msgstr "配置时出了差错，现在无法正常启动。有什么办法可以修复吗？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:671
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You either forgot (or misspelled) the entry in [.filename]#/boot/loader."
"conf#, or there are errors in your [.filename]#/etc/fstab# file.  These are "
"usually easy to fix.  During system startup, when the boot process stops and "
"prompts for single-user mode (for example after a failed mount or `fsck` "
"error), press kbd:[Enter] to get to the default single user shell.  Then "
"locate the root of the problem:"
msgstr "可能是忘记了在 [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# 中添加条目（或拼错了），也可能是 [.filename]#/etc/fstab# 文件中有错误。这些问题通常很容易修复。系统启动时，如果启动过程停止并提示进入单用户模式（例如，挂载失败或出现 `fsck` 错误后），按 kbd:[Enter] 进入默认的单用户 shell。然后找出问题所在："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:675
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# cat /boot/loader.conf\n"
msgstr "# cat /boot/loader.conf\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:678
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ensure that the following line exists and is spelled correctly:"
msgstr "确认存在以下行且拼写正确："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:686
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the `geom_journal_load` entry is missing or misspelled, the journaled "
"devices are never created.  Load the module manually, mount all partitions, "
"and continue with multi-user boot:"
msgstr "如果缺少 `geom_journal_load` 条目或其拼写有误，就不会创建日志设备。手动加载模块，挂载所有分区，然后继续启动到多用户模式："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:697
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"GEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 2948326772: ada0p4 contains journal.\n"
"GEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 3193218002: ada0p5 contains journal.\n"
"GEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 2948326772: ada0p2 contains data.\n"
"GEOM_JOURNAL: Journal ada0p2 clean.\n"
"GEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 3193218002: ada0p3 contains data.\n"
"GEOM_JOURNAL: Journal ada0p3 clean.\n"
msgstr "GEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 2948326772: ada0p4 contains journal.\nGEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 3193218002: ada0p5 contains journal.\nGEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 2948326772: ada0p2 contains data.\nGEOM_JOURNAL: Journal ada0p2 clean.\nGEOM_JOURNAL: Journal 3193218002: ada0p3 contains data.\nGEOM_JOURNAL: Journal ada0p3 clean.\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:701
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# mount -a\n"
"# exit\n"
"(boot continues)\n"
msgstr "# mount -a\n# exit\n(boot continues)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:706
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If, on the other hand, this entry is correct, have a look at [.filename]#/"
"etc/fstab#.  You will probably find a misspelled or missing entry.  In this "
"case, mount all remaining partitions by hand and continue with the multi-"
"user boot."
msgstr "另一方面，如果该条目正确，请检查 [.filename]#/etc/fstab#。很可能是条目拼写有误或缺失。在这种情况下，手动挂载其余分区，然后继续启动到多用户模式。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:707
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Can I remove journaling and return to my standard file system with Soft Updates?"
msgstr "可以移除日志功能并恢复为使用 Soft Updates 的标准文件系统吗？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:712
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Sure.  Use the following procedure, which reverses the changes.  The "
"partitions you created for the journal providers can then be used for other "
"purposes, if you so wish."
msgstr "当然可以。使用以下步骤即可撤销所做的更改。如果愿意，之后可以将为日志提供者创建的分区用于其他用途。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:714
#, fuzzy
msgid "Login as `root` and switch to single user mode:"
msgstr "以 `root` 身份登录并切换到单用户模式："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:721
#, fuzzy
msgid "Unmount the journaled partitions:"
msgstr "卸载带日志的分区："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:728
#, fuzzy
msgid "Synchronize the journals:"
msgstr "同步日志："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:732
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# gjournal sync\n"
msgstr "# gjournal sync\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:735
#, fuzzy
msgid "Stop the journaling providers:"
msgstr "停止日志提供者："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:740
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# gjournal stop ada0p2.journal\n"
"# gjournal stop ada0p3.journal\n"
msgstr "# gjournal stop ada0p2.journal\n# gjournal stop ada0p3.journal\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:744
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next step should be done with unloaded gjournal kernel module.  If the "
"following command fails:"
msgstr "接下来的步骤应在卸载 gjournal 内核模块后执行。如果以下命令失败："

#. type: source
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:749
#, fuzzy
msgid "...  # gjournal unload ..."
msgstr "...  # gjournal unload ..."

#. type: source
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:751
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"ensure that the following line exists in [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# and "
"is spelled correctly:"
msgstr "请确认 [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# 中存在以下行且拼写正确："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:755
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "geom_journal_load=\"NO\"\n"
msgstr "geom_journal_load=\"YES\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:758
#, fuzzy
msgid "Reboot your desktop without gjournal kernel module:"
msgstr "不加载 gjournal 内核模块，重新启动桌面系统："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:765
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Boot into single-user mode again. Clear the journaling metadata from all the "
"devices used:"
msgstr "再次进入单用户模式。清除所有相关设备上的日志元数据："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:772
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# gjournal clear ada0p2\n"
"# gjournal clear ada0p3\n"
"# gjournal clear ada0p4\n"
"# gjournal clear ada0p5\n"
msgstr "# gjournal clear ada0p2\n# gjournal clear ada0p3\n# gjournal clear ada0p4\n# gjournal clear ada0p5\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:775
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Clear the file system journaling flag, and restore the Soft Updates flags:"
msgstr "清除文件系统日志标志，并恢复 Soft Updates 标志："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:782
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# tunefs -J disable -n enable -j enable ada0p2\n"
"tunefs: soft updates journaling set\n"
"tunefs: gjournal cleared\n"
"tunefs: soft updates set\n"
msgstr "# tunefs -J disable -n enable -j enable ada0p2\ntunefs: soft updates journaling set\ntunefs: gjournal cleared\ntunefs: soft updates set\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:787
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# tunefs -J disable -n enable -j enable ada0p3\n"
"tunefs: soft updates journaling set\n"
"tunefs: gjournal cleared\n"
"tunefs: soft updates set\n"
msgstr "# tunefs -J disable -n enable -j enable ada0p3\ntunefs: soft updates journaling set\ntunefs: gjournal cleared\ntunefs: soft updates set\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:790
#, fuzzy
msgid "Remount the old devices by hand:"
msgstr "手动重新挂载原来的设备："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:795
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# mount -o rw /dev/ada0p2 /var\n"
"# mount -o rw /dev/ada0p3 /usr\n"
msgstr "# mount -o rw /dev/ada0p2 /var\n# mount -o rw /dev/ada0p3 /usr\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:798
#, fuzzy
msgid "Edit [.filename]#/etc/fstab# and restore it to its original state:"
msgstr "编辑 [.filename]#/etc/fstab#，将其恢复到原来的状态："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:803
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"/dev/ada0p2     /usr            ufs     rw      2       2\n"
"/dev/ada0p3     /var            ufs     rw      2       2\n"
msgstr "/dev/ada0p2     /usr            ufs     rw      2       2\n/dev/ada0p3     /var            ufs     rw      2       2\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:806
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Finally, edit [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf#, remove the entry that loads "
"the `geom_journal` module (or re-enable it if gjournal is still required for "
"other partitions), and reboot."
msgstr "最后，编辑 [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf#，删除用于加载 `geom_journal` 模块的条目（如果其他分区仍需要 gjournal，则重新启用该条目），然后重新启动。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:807
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "How do I temporarily boot without GEOM journaling?"
msgstr "如何在不使用 GEOM 日志的情况下临时启动？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:810
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To boot the system without GEOM journaling, prevent the journal module from "
"loading during startup."
msgstr "要在不使用 GEOM 日志的情况下启动系统，请阻止日志模块在启动期间加载。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:812
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Comment out or remove the following line from [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# "
"and reboot:"
msgstr "从 [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# 中注释掉或删除以下行，然后重新启动："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:820
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After booting without GEOM journaling, journaled devices (`*.journal`) will "
"not be created.  File Systems must be mounted using their original (non-"
"journaled) providers, or mounted manually as needed for recovery or "
"maintenance."
msgstr "在不使用 GEOM 日志的情况下启动后，不会创建带日志的设备（`*.journal`）。必须使用原始的（非日志）提供者挂载文件系统，或根据需要手动挂载以进行恢复或维护。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:822
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This method does not modify on-disk journal metadata and can be safely used "
"for troubleshooting."
msgstr "此方法不会修改磁盘上的日志元数据，可安全用于故障排除。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:823
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Can I resize a GEOM journal after it has been created?"
msgstr "创建 GEOM 日志后可以调整其大小吗？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:826
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"No. A GEOM journal cannot be resized in place after it has been created."
msgstr "不可以。创建 GEOM 日志后无法就地调整其大小。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:830
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The journal size is fixed at the time the journal is labeled.  To change the "
"journal size, GEOM journaling must be removed and reconfigured with a new "
"journal provider of the desired size.  For file systems containing data, "
"this requires unmounting the file system and recreating the journal using "
"appropriately sized providers, as described earlier in this article."
msgstr "日志大小在标记日志时即已固定。要更改日志大小，必须移除并重新配置 GEOM 日志，并使用所需大小的新日志提供者。对于包含数据的文件系统，需要先卸载文件系统，再使用大小合适的提供者重新创建日志，具体步骤如本文前文所述。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:832
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Plan journal sizes conservatively to accommodate peak write activity, as "
"resizing requires reinitialization of the journal configuration."
msgstr "规划日志大小时应留有余量，以满足写入活动高峰的需要，因为调整大小需要重新初始化日志配置。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:833
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "What happens after an unclean shutdown or power failure?"
msgstr "非正常关机或断电后会发生什么？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:836
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After an unclean shutdown or power failure, GEOM journaling and Soft Updates "
"with journaling replay the pending journal records during the next boot to "
"return the file system to a consistent state."
msgstr "非正常关机或断电后，GEOM 日志和带日志的 Soft Updates 会在下次启动时重放待处理的日志记录，使文件系统恢复到一致状态。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:839
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the journal replay completes successfully, the file system is mounted "
"normally and no full file system check is required.  Journal replay "
"typically takes only a few seconds and depends on the amount of recent write "
"activity rather than the size of the file system."
msgstr "如果日志重放成功，文件系统会正常挂载，无需执行完整的文件系统检查。日志重放通常只需几秒钟，耗时取决于近期写入活动的数量，而不是文件系统的大小。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:841
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A full file system check may still be required in rare cases, such as when "
"underlying storage errors are detected or the journal itself is inconsistent."
msgstr "在少数情况下，例如检测到底层存储错误或日志本身不一致时，仍可能需要执行完整的文件系统检查。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:842
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "How does GEOM journaling interact with fsck?"
msgstr "GEOM 日志如何与 fsck 交互？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:845
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"GEOM journaling and Soft Updates with journaling interact with `fsck_ffs(8)` "
"in different ways, reflecting their different integration levels in the "
"FreeBSD storage stack."
msgstr "GEOM 日志和带日志的 Soft Updates 与 `fsck_ffs(8)` 的交互方式不同，这反映了它们在 FreeBSD 存储栈中的集成程度不同。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:850
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For GEOM journaling, crash recovery is performed by the GEOM framework "
"itself.  During system startup, the `geom_journal` class detects journal "
"metadata and replays any pending journal records while the provider is being "
"tasted by GEOM, before the journaled device becomes visible to higher layers "
"of the system.  If journal replay completes successfully, the file system is "
"returned to a consistent state and the UFS superblock is updated to indicate "
"that no file system check is required.  When `fsck_ffs(8)` is later invoked "
"during boot, it reads this state from the superblock and skips the file "
"system check."
msgstr "对于 GEOM 日志，崩溃恢复由 GEOM 框架本身执行。系统启动期间，`geom_journal` 类会检测日志元数据，并在 GEOM 对提供者进行探测时重放任何待处理的日志记录，此时带日志的设备尚未对系统的上层可见。如果日志重放成功，文件系统将恢复到一致状态，并更新 UFS 超级块以表明无需进行文件系统检查。启动过程中稍后调用 `fsck_ffs(8)` 时，它会从超级块读取此状态并跳过文件系统检查。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:855
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For Soft Updates with journaling, recovery is initiated by `fsck_ffs(8)` "
"itself.  During the file system check phase at boot time, `fsck_ffs(8)` "
"detects that the file system supports Soft Updates with journaling and "
"invokes the journal replay logic.  If journal replay reports that the file "
"system is consistent, `fsck_ffs(8)` terminates early without performing a "
"full check.  If journal replay cannot complete successfully, a traditional "
"file system check is performed."
msgstr "对于带日志的 Soft Updates，恢复由 `fsck_ffs(8)` 本身启动。启动时进入文件系统检查阶段后，`fsck_ffs(8)` 会检测文件系统是否支持带日志的 Soft Updates，并调用日志重放逻辑。如果日志重放报告文件系统处于一致状态，`fsck_ffs(8)` 会提前退出，不执行完整检查。如果日志重放无法成功完成，则会执行传统的文件系统检查。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:857
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"As a result, the recovery path during system startup depends on the "
"journaling mechanism in use, as illustrated by the following boot sequence:"
msgstr "因此，系统启动期间的恢复路径取决于所使用的日志机制，如以下启动顺序所示："

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:884
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Firmware / Boot Loader\n"
"        |\n"
"        v\n"
"Kernel initialization\n"
"        |\n"
"        v\n"
"GEOM framework (provider tasting)\n"
"        |\n"
"        +--> GEOM journaling (gjournal)\n"
"        |       - Journal replay occurs here\n"
"        |       - Filesystem consistency is restored\n"
"        |       - Superblock is updated\n"
"        |\n"
"        v\n"
"Filesystem check phase (fsck_ffs)\n"
"        |\n"
"        +--> Soft Updates with journaling\n"
"        |       - Journal replay initiated by fsck\n"
"        |       - fsck exits early if consistent\n"
"        |\n"
"        v\n"
"Filesystem mount\n"
"        |\n"
"        v\n"
"Normal system operation\n"
msgstr "固件 / 引导加载器\n        |\n        v\n内核初始化\n        |\n        v\nGEOM 框架（提供者探测）\n        |\n        +--> GEOM 日志（gjournal）\n        |       - 日志重放在此处进行\n        |       - 文件系统一致性得到恢复\n        |       - 超级块得到更新\n        |\n        v\n文件系统检查阶段（fsck_ffs）\n        |\n        +--> 带日志的 Soft Updates\n        |       - 由 fsck 启动日志重放\n        |       - 如果文件系统一致，fsck 会提前退出\n        |\n        v\n挂载文件系统\n        |\n        v\n系统正常运行\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:888
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`fsck_ffs(8)` is still used when journal replay cannot be completed, when "
"underlying storage errors are detected, or during periodic manual or "
"scheduled file system checks.  GEOM journaling reduces recovery time after "
"crashes but does not replace `fsck_ffs(8)` entirely."
msgstr "如果无法完成日志重放、检测到底层存储错误，或在定期手动检查或计划的文件系统检查期间，仍会使用 `fsck_ffs(8)`。GEOM 日志可以缩短崩溃后的恢复时间，但不能完全取代 `fsck_ffs(8)`。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:889
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Why does `gjournal clear` report \"Operation not permitted\" even in single-user mode?"
msgstr "为什么即使在单用户模式下，`gjournal clear` 仍会报告 \"Operation not permitted\"？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:894
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In GEOM, the same underlying storage can be exposed through multiple "
"provider names at the same time.  For example, a partition may be visible "
"both under its disk-based name (e.g. `vtbd0p7`) and under a GPT label (e.g. "
"`/dev/gpt/labelname`).  These are different GEOM providers referring to the "
"same physical storage."
msgstr "在 GEOM 中，同一底层存储可以同时通过多个提供者名称公开。例如，一个分区可能既以基于磁盘的名称（如 `vtbd0p7`）显示，也以 GPT 标签（如 `/dev/gpt/labelname`）显示。这些是不同的 GEOM 提供者，但指向同一物理存储。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:897
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When `gjournal stop` or `gjournal clear` is executed on one provider name, "
"the GEOM framework may immediately detect the journal metadata again through "
"another provider name during the tasting process.  As a result, the journal "
"is re-attached automatically, and attempts to clear its metadata fail with "
"an \"Operation not permitted\" error."
msgstr "在某个提供者名称上执行 `gjournal stop` 或 `gjournal clear` 时，GEOM 框架可能会在探测过程中立即通过另一个提供者名称再次检测到日志元数据。因此，日志会自动重新附加，清除其元数据的尝试则会因 \"Operation not permitted\" 错误而失败。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:900
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It is technically possible to suppress this behavior by disabling GEOM "
"tasting or by preventing the creation of alternative provider names, but "
"doing so is strongly discouraged.  Such changes may negatively affect other "
"GEOM classes and system components that rely on normal provider discovery."
msgstr "虽然在技术上可以通过禁用 GEOM 探测或阻止创建备用提供者名称来抑制此行为，但强烈不建议这样做。这些更改可能会对依赖正常提供者发现机制的其他 GEOM 类和系统组件造成负面影响。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:903
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For this reason, the recommended and safe procedure is to unload the "
"`geom_journal` module entirely before removing journal metadata, as "
"described earlier in this article.  With the module unloaded, no tasting "
"occurs and the journal cannot be re-attached, allowing `gjournal clear` to "
"complete successfully."
msgstr "因此，推荐且安全的做法是在移除日志元数据之前彻底卸载 `geom_journal` 模块，具体说明见本文前文。卸载模块后不会进行探测，日志也无法重新附加，因此 `gjournal clear` 可以成功完成。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:904
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Can GEOM journaling be used on the root file system?"
msgstr "可以在根文件系统上使用 GEOM 日志吗？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:907
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Yes. GEOM journaling can be used on the root file system, but it requires "
"additional care during system configuration."
msgstr "可以。在根文件系统上使用 GEOM 日志是可行的，但系统配置时需要格外谨慎。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:910
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The GEOM journal module must be loaded early during the boot process so that "
"the journaled root device is available before the root file system is "
"mounted.  Misconfiguration may prevent the system from booting normally, so "
"this setup is generally recommended only for experienced users who fully "
"understand the boot sequence and recovery procedures."
msgstr "必须在引导过程的早期加载 GEOM 日志模块，以便在挂载根文件系统之前，使启用日志的根设备可用。配置错误可能导致系统无法正常引导，因此通常只建议充分了解引导顺序和恢复流程的有经验用户采用此配置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:912
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For these reasons, GEOM journaling is more commonly applied to non-root file "
"systems such as `/usr` and `/var`."
msgstr "因此，GEOM 日志更常用于 `/usr` 和 `/var` 等非根文件系统。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:913
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "What are the performance implications of using GEOM journaling?"
msgstr "使用 GEOM 日志会对性能产生什么影响？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:917
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"GEOM journaling introduces additional write I/O because all write operations "
"are first recorded in the journal before being committed to the data "
"provider.  This results in increased write latency and higher overall write "
"amplification compared to non-journaled file systems."
msgstr "GEOM 日志会增加写入 I/O，因为所有写操作在提交到数据提供者之前，都会先记录到日志中。与未启用日志的文件系统相比，这会增加写入延迟和总体写入放大。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:921
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Read performance is typically unaffected.  The performance impact is most "
"noticeable on write-heavy workloads and depends on journal size, placement, "
"and the speed of the underlying storage.  Using a sufficiently sized journal "
"and fast storage for the journal provider minimizes performance penalties."
msgstr "读取性能通常不会受到影响。性能影响在写入密集型工作负载下最明显，并取决于日志大小、存放位置以及底层存储的速度。为日志提供者配置足够大的日志空间并使用快速存储，可以最大限度地减少性能损失。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:922
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Can GEOM journaling be used together with other GEOM classes?"
msgstr "GEOM 日志可以与其他 GEOM 类一起使用吗？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:925
#, fuzzy
msgid "Yes. GEOM journaling can be stacked with other GEOM classes."
msgstr "可以。GEOM 日志可以与其他 GEOM 类堆叠使用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:928
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When used together, GEOM journaling typically operates on top of providers "
"created by other GEOM classes such as `gmirror(8)` or `graid3(8)`.  The "
"order of stacking is important and should follow the documented layering "
"requirements of the involved GEOM classes."
msgstr "组合使用时，GEOM 日志通常运行在其他 GEOM 类创建的提供者之上，例如 `gmirror(8)` 或 `graid3(8)`。堆叠顺序很重要，应遵循所涉及 GEOM 类的文档要求。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:930
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"GEOM journaling maintains file system consistency across the stacked "
"providers, but it does not replace redundancy or error detection provided by "
"other GEOM classes."
msgstr "GEOM 日志可在堆叠的提供者之间维持文件系统一致性，但不能取代其他 GEOM 类提供的冗余或错误检测功能。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:931
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Can GEOM journaling and Soft Updates be enabled at the same time?"
msgstr "可以同时启用 GEOM 日志和 Soft Updates 吗？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:934
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"No. GEOM journaling and Soft Updates must not be enabled at the same time on "
"the same file system."
msgstr "不可以。在同一文件系统上不得同时启用 GEOM 日志和 Soft Updates。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:937
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"GEOM journaling requires exclusive control over write ordering and "
"consistency guarantees.  If Soft Updates are enabled together with GEOM "
"journaling, the file system may behave unpredictably and data integrity "
"cannot be guaranteed."
msgstr "GEOM 日志需要独占控制写入顺序并提供一致性保证。如果同时启用了 Soft Updates 和 GEOM 日志，文件系统可能会出现不可预测的行为，且无法保证数据完整性。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:939
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When using GEOM journaling, Soft Updates must be disabled on the affected "
"file system, as described earlier in this article."
msgstr "使用 GEOM 日志时，必须在受影响的文件系统上禁用 Soft Updates，具体说明见本文前文。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:941
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "What is the difference between Soft Updates and Soft Updates with Journaling?"
msgstr "Soft Updates 与带日志的 Soft Updates 有什么区别？"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:944
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Both Soft Updates and Soft Updates with Journaling are designed to maintain "
"file system consistency, but they use different mechanisms and behave "
"differently after a system crash."
msgstr "Soft Updates 和带日志的 Soft Updates 都旨在维持文件系统一致性，但使用的机制不同，系统崩溃后的行为也不同。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:948
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"_Soft Updates_ ensure consistency by carefully ordering metadata writes in "
"memory so that only safe states are written to disk.  If a crash occurs, any "
"metadata updates that have not yet been written are simply lost, leaving the "
"file system in a consistent but possibly older state.  However, resource "
"accounting may be temporarily inaccurate, and a full `fsck_ffs(8)` run is "
"required to reclaim unused blocks and inodes."
msgstr "__Soft Updates__ 通过在内存中谨慎安排元数据写入顺序，确保只有安全状态会写入磁盘。如果发生崩溃，尚未写入的元数据更新会直接丢失，文件系统仍保持一致，但状态可能较旧。不过，资源统计可能会暂时不准确，并且需要完整运行一次 `fsck_ffs(8)`，以回收未使用的块和 inode。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:952
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"_Soft Updates with Journaling_ build on top of _Soft Updates_ by adding a "
"metadata journal stored within the file system.  Metadata changes are first "
"recorded in the journal and are replayed automatically during the next boot "
"after an unclean shutdown.  This allows the file system to be restored to a "
"consistent state quickly, usually without requiring a full `fsck_ffs(8)` run."
msgstr "__带日志的 Soft Updates__ 在 __Soft Updates__ 的基础上增加了存储在文件系统内的元数据日志。元数据更改会先记录到日志中，并在非正常关机后的下次引导期间自动重放。这样可以快速将文件系统恢复到一致状态，通常无需完整运行一次 `fsck_ffs(8)`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/gjournal-desktop/_index.adoc:954
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In short, _Soft Updates_ provide consistency without a journal, while _Soft "
"Updates with Journaling_ add fast and automatic recovery after crashes at "
"the cost of additional disk space and minor performance overhead."
msgstr "简而言之，__Soft Updates__ 无需日志即可提供一致性，而 __带日志的 Soft Updates__ 则以额外的磁盘空间和少量性能开销为代价，在崩溃后实现快速自动恢复。"

